  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report 2023's own audited Solo Balance Sheet and Solo Profit and Loss Account (headed 'Balance Sheet as at 31 December 2023' / 'Profit and Loss Account', The Premier Bank PLC - the company converted its legal suffix from 'Limited' to 'PLC' this year). A separate, materially higher, Consolidated Balance Sheet exists in the same report (Total Assets 414,966.38m vs this Solo figure of 414,401.58m). Interest income (20,834,289,731) and net interest income (4,150,391,460) are confirmed directly from the raw Solo Profit and Loss Account, matching the five-year table exactly. Reserve fund = Statutory reserve (9,749.46) + Other reserve (61.93) + General reserve (300.00) + Retained earnings (4,908.15) = 15,019.54, matching the 'Reserve and Surplus' figure in this and the FY2024 report's five-year tables exactly; Paid-up capital (12,334.31) + Reserve fund (15,019.54) = 27,353.85 = Total Equity exactly. Balance-sheet identity confirmed to within Tk.0.01m. Total Operating Income/Expense show a small restatement: this report's own five-year table states 17,664.26/8,518.43 for FY2023, while the FY2024 report's comparative shows 17,498.46/8,352.63 (both differ by the same Tk.165.80m, so Operating Profit of 9,145.82 and everything below are unaffected - a pure presentational gross/net change, not a profitability restatement); contemporaneous figures kept. NPL% (4.99%) already reported on the 'including OBU & Staff loan' basis this year. ldr_pct (80.87%) is kept as directly reported ('Credit to Deposit Ratio (As per Bangladesh Bank)') rather than calculated, because it uses Bangladesh Bank's specific regulatory Advance-Deposit Ratio formula, which differs materially from a simple gross_loans/total_deposits division (289,392.27/316,870.64=91.33% - a 10.5pp gap from the reported 80.87%); this is a formula difference in the numerator/denominator definition, not a data error, and is why this is the only year in the series where ldr_pct is 'reported' rather than 'calculated'.",
